<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-1" name=3D"story-1" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>1. CMS makes active verification =
a condition of subsidized Exchange enrollment</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">On October 23, CMS proposed requiring =
Exchanges to verify household income and size, citizenship or eligible noncit=
izen status, other qualifying coverage and residency before providing advance=
 premium-tax-credit payments or cost-sharing reductions. Starting with 2028 c=
overage, existing members would have to return annually and confirm their inf=
ormation to retain financial assistance; otherwise, they could be automatical=
ly re-enrolled only without subsidies. The first proposed pre-open-enrollment=
 verification period would begin August 1, 2027. (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.=
gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/exchange-pre-eligibility-verification-proposed-rule-=
cms-9873-p" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS, <em>Excha=
nge Pre-Eligibility Verification Proposed Rule</em>, October 23, 2026</a>) (<=
a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/exchange-pre-eligibility-v=
erification-proposed-rule-cms-9873-p" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:=
underline;">cms.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS estimates that the proposal would =
reduce annual Exchange enrollment by approximately 332,500, decrease APTC spe=
nding by $7.6 billion beginning in 2028 and increase average premiums by 0.4%=
, or $2.89 per member per month, because administrative barriers would dispro=
portionately deter younger and healthier consumers. (<a href=3D"https://publi=
c-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-21891.pdf" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-=
decoration:underline;">Federal Register public-inspection document, <em>CMS-9=
873-P</em>, October 23, 2026</a>) (<a href=3D"https://public-inspection.feder=
alregister.gov/2026-21891.pdf" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underli=
ne;">public-inspection.federalregister.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">This extends the September membership-=
removal thesis into a permanent annual operating model. Marketplace carriers =
now face more churn, delayed subsidy activation, retroactive enrollment trans=
actions and less predictable risk pools=E2=80=94not merely tighter broker con=
trols. Premium revenue should decline with enrollment, although CMS acknowled=
ges that claims may also fall and does not quantify the net margin effect.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The near-term technology demand is for=
 eligibility orchestration, document collection, identity and residency verif=
ication, broker outreach and enrollment reconciliation. Providers face a smal=
ler but meaningful 2028 increase in coverage gaps, bad debt and delayed care =
if eligible consumers fail to complete verification.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether CMS reduces friction for passi=
ve renewals and how Exchanges operationalize retroactive subsidies and pended=
 plan selections without generating avoidable claims and premium-reconciliati=
on errors.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-2" name=3D"story-2" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>2. Molina quantifies a narrow Med=
icaid rate-trend crossover</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Molina reported a 93% third-quarter Me=
dicaid medical-cost ratio and said elevated medical trend appears to be plate=
auing as recent state rate actions begin to close the funding gap. Management=
=E2=80=99s preliminary 2027 assumptions place Medicaid rates at approximately=
 6% and medical-cost trend at 5.5%-6%; it also expects enrollment pressure fr=
om work requirements and more frequent eligibility reverifications. (<a href=
=3D"https://molinahealthcare.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/m=
olina-healthcare-reports-third-quarter-2026-financial-results" style=3D"color=
:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Molina Healthcare, <em>Third Quarter 202=
6 Financial Results</em>, October 21, 2026</a>; <a href=3D"https://www.fool.c=
om/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/22/molina-healthcare-moh-q3-2026-earning=
s-call-transcript/" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">earnin=
gs-call transcript, October 22, 2026</a>) (<a href=3D"https://molinahealthcar=
e.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/molina-healthcare-reports-th=
ird-quarter-2026-financial-results?utm_source=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9=
a;text-decoration:underline;">molinahealthcare.gcs-web.com</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Elevance provided corroborating, thoug=
h less specific, evidence: premium increases offset membership attrition, whi=
le Medicaid enrollment fell 4.9% year over year. Elevance=E2=80=99s consolida=
ted benefit ratio improved primarily because of Medicare Advantage and indivi=
dual ACA performance, so its release does not establish a fully recovered Med=
icaid margin. (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1156039/000=
115603926000068/a3q2026elvearningsrelease.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-de=
coration:underline;">Elevance Health, <em>Third Quarter 2026 Results</em>, Oc=
tober 21, 2026</a>) (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/11560=
39/000115603926000068/a3q2026elvearningsrelease.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;t=
ext-decoration:underline;">sec.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The new evidence changes the Medicaid =
thesis from =E2=80=9Crates should eventually catch up=E2=80=9D to =E2=80=9Cra=
tes may approximately match trend in 2027.=E2=80=9D That is an inflection, no=
t normalization: a zero-to-50-basis-point spread leaves little protection aga=
inst pharmacy, outpatient or acuity surprises.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Plans should continue prioritizing acu=
ity detection, eligibility forecasting, payment integrity and high-cost case =
management rather than assuming broad margin expansion. Providers should expe=
ct continued contracting discipline even where state rates improve, because m=
embership attrition and mix changes can offset nominal rate gains.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether fourth-quarter utilization rem=
ains within Molina=E2=80=99s 5.5%-6% trend assumption and whether state rate =
updates include retrospective relief or only prospective increases.</p>
