<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-3" name=3D"story-3" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>3. Self-funded employers push pri=
or-authorization infrastructure beyond CMS-0057</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS and the Department of Labor announ=
ced on October 21 that Amazon, Axon, Google, Meta and Oracle support making t=
he capabilities developed under the 2025 Prior Authorization Pledge available=
 to self-funded employer plans. Those capabilities include FHIR-based electro=
nic prior authorization, fewer services requiring authorization, greater tran=
sparency and more real-time decisions. The employer statement is voluntary an=
d does not itself impose deadlines or performance standards. (<a href=3D"http=
s://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/leading-employers-back-expansion-elec=
tronic-prior-authorization-self-funded-health-plans" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;t=
ext-decoration:underline;">CMS, <em>Leading Employers Back Expansion of Elect=
ronic Prior Authorization to Self-Funded Health Plans</em>, October 21, 2026<=
/a>) (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/leading-employer=
s-back-expansion-electronic-prior-authorization-self-funded-health-plans?utm_=
source=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">cms.gov</=
a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The regulated-plan API build is becomi=
ng a commercial platform expectation. Large employers do not want providers s=
witching between electronic workflows for Medicare Advantage or Medicaid pati=
ents and manual workflows for employees administered by the same carrier or T=
PA.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">This strengthens demand for reusable p=
ayer APIs, authorization-rule engines, clinical-document exchange and workflo=
w integration. However, the immediate revenue opportunity remains dependent o=
n TPA contract amendments and employer purchasing decisions; a pledge without=
 adoption metrics should not be treated as equivalent to CMS-0057 compliance.=
</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether national TPAs commit to common=
 deployment dates and disclose self-funded authorization volumes, decision ti=
mes and real-time approval rates.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-4" name=3D"story-4" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>4. Regional integration advances =
through both ownership and shared platforms</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Horizon Mutual Holdings confirmed an a=
greement to acquire Summit Health New Jersey, including New Jersey CityMD sit=
es, subject to regulatory review. The transaction would place a major multisp=
ecialty and urgent-care network under the state=E2=80=99s dominant Blue plan.=
 (<a href=3D"https://binje.com/sectors/health-care/horizon-bcbs-to-purchase-s=
ummit-health-in-billion-dollar-deal/" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:=
underline;">BINJE, <em>Horizon BCBS to Purchase Summit Health in Billion-Doll=
ar Deal</em>, October 21, 2026</a>) (<a href=3D"https://binje.com/sectors/hea=
lth-care/horizon-bcbs-to-purchase-summit-health-in-billion-dollar-deal/?utm_s=
ource=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">binje.com<=
/a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Separately, Kaiser Permanente-backed R=
isant Health signed a definitive agreement to add INTEGRIS Health as its thir=
d member system after Geisinger and Cone Health. INTEGRIS operates 10 acute a=
nd 10 specialty hospitals and will retain its brand and leadership while adop=
ting Risant=E2=80=99s value-based-care and technology capabilities. (<a href=
=3D"https://integrishealth.org/resources/news/2026/october/integris-health-to=
-become-part-of-risant-health" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underli=
ne;">INTEGRIS Health, <em>INTEGRIS Health to Become Part of Risant Health</em=
>, October 21, 2026</a>) (<a href=3D"https://integrishealth.org/resources/new=
s/2026/october/integris-health-to-become-part-of-risant-health?utm_source=3Do=
penai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">integrishealth.org<=
/a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Horizon is pursuing direct capture of =
referral, ambulatory and site-of-care economics; Risant is scaling a common o=
perating platform across locally branded systems. Both models increase enterp=
rise standardization and favor vendors capable of systemwide deployment, but =
they also concentrate purchasing authority and raise displacement risk for po=
int solutions.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Regulatory conditions on Horizon=E2=80=
=99s acquisition and evidence that Risant can reproduce its claimed operating=
 improvements outside Geisinger and Cone=E2=80=99s markets.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-5" name=3D"story-5" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>5. DOJ puts a defined price range=
 on voluntary FCA resolution</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">DOJ and HHS launched a six-month healt=
hcare False Claims Act self-disclosure pilot on October 22. Companies must pr=
ovide relevant facts and documents, describe remediation and repay the govern=
ment using a 1.25-to-1.6 multiplier. In exchange, participants may receive a =
coordinated release under the federal FCA and specified HHS administrative au=
thorities. Submissions are accepted through April 22, 2027; potential crimina=
l conduct follows separate disclosure procedures. (<a href=3D"https://www.jus=
tice.gov/opa/pr/justice-departments-civil-division-and-department-health-huma=
n-services-announce-anti-fraud" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underl=
ine;">Department of Justice, <em>Healthcare False Claims Act Self-Disclosure =
Pilot Program</em>, October 22, 2026</a>) (<a href=3D"https://www.justice.gov=
/opa/pr/justice-departments-civil-division-and-department-health-human-servic=
es-announce-anti-fraud?utm_source=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decor=
ation:underline;">justice.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The program gives plans, providers and=
 acquirers a more calculable alternative to waiting for whistleblower litigat=
ion or enforcement. It is particularly relevant to unsupported coding, risk-a=
djustment deletions, billing errors and successor liabilities discovered duri=
ng integration.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Expect stronger demand for retrospecti=
ve claims analytics, coding validation, defensible sampling and transaction d=
iligence. The pathway reduces uncertainty=E2=80=94not liability=E2=80=94and r=
ewards rapid remediation before an issue expands in duration, value or senior=
-management involvement.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether DOJ accepts disclosures involv=
ing conduct already subject to payer audits or government data analysis, and =
how coordinated releases address successor liability.</p>
